---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../../components/PageHero.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../lib/paths";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial standards, corrections & privacy"
  description="How to read Independent Observer status labels, request corrections, understand browser-local tools, and ask about reuse or disclosures."
  currentPath="/governance/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Standards & trust"
    title="Editorial standards, corrections & privacy"
    description="A compact guide to editorial standards, corrections, privacy, reuse, and disclosures."
  />
  <section class="section section-white">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <p class="review-date"><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> 8 October 2026</p>
      <h2>Editorial standards</h2>
      <p>
        Independent Observer separates evidence, interpretation, and proposals. Public records
        identify sources and limitations where available. Working papers, concept previews, and
        books in editorial development retain their status labels; availability on this site does
        not imply peer review or a finished book.
      </p>
      <h2 id="status-labels">Status labels</h2>
      <p>
        Status labels describe what a reader can use now; they do not grade the quality of an idea
        or substitute for independent review.
      </p>
      <dl class="status-definitions">
        <dt>Working-paper summary</dt>
        <dd>
          A short explanation of an author working paper. The complete manuscript may be available
          separately; follow the links on the page.
        </dd>
        <dt>Full working paper</dt>
        <dd>
          The complete site reading edition of a work in progress. It has not been externally peer
          reviewed unless the page records otherwise.
        </dd>
        <dt>Published article / published document</dt>
        <dd>
          An article or document available to read here. Publication on this site does not imply
          external peer review.
        </dd>
        <dt>Research preview / media preview</dt>
        <dd>
          An outline, early article, or audio or video preview. The work may change as research and
          production continue.
        </dd>
        <dt>In editorial development / publication pending</dt>
        <dd>
          The referenced work is being prepared and is not yet available as a complete publication
          on this site.
        </dd>
        <dt>Reference document / guide</dt>
        <dd>
          Source material, contextual records, or an explanation of a method. These are not new
          research findings.
        </dd>
        <dt>Public learning exercise</dt>
        <dd>
          A teaching example for testing a method. Hypothetical examples are identified and are not
          empirical results.
        </dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
        Older records may use more specific labels such as author working paper, public reading
        copy, or concept preview. Check each page’s availability notes to see whether it contains a
        summary, a full text, or an external manuscript link.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        To question a claim or report an error, use the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}
          >contact page</a
        >. Include the page address, the passage, and evidence supporting a correction. Public paper
        revisions are listed when recorded. An approved correction is marked in the affected page’s <strong
          >Revision history</strong
        > with its date, change, reason, and a link to the affected section. The same paper correction
        also appears in the <a href={sitePath("/latest/#latest-revisions-title")}>revision log</a>;
        software and interface changes appear in <a href={sitePath("/whats-new/")}>What’s New</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Correction inquiries have no guaranteed response time. Include the passage and supporting
        evidence so the author can assess the issue.
      </p>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Search runs in your browser after downloading a public index. Search queries are not
        submitted to a search server. Reading lists, tags, and reading status use local browser
        storage; you can clear saved items or export them. Imported reading lists are processed on
        your device.
      </p>
      <p>
        The contact page prepares an email draft or copies text for your webmail. It does not submit
        a form to this website. Your email provider handles messages you send. Visiting the website
        still requires ordinary network requests to its hosting provider. External links open
        services with their own privacy practices.
      </p>
      <h3>Reader list and hosting</h3>
      <p>
        The reader-list links currently lead to Substack. This site does not collect the email
        address itself; Substack handles any subscription under its own privacy practices. The
        primary site is hosted on Vercel, so ordinary requests to that deployment are processed
        through Vercel’s infrastructure. A public, noindex fallback is also deployed through GitHub
        Pages; requests to that fallback are processed through GitHub’s infrastructure.
      </p>
      <h3>Analytics, cookies, and browser storage</h3>
      <p>
        The site ships browser-side event and article-scroll instrumentation, but it has no
        production analytics provider or outbound analytics transport. Its production event adapter
        is a no-op, so analytics events do not leave the browser. The site code does not set
        cookies. It does use local storage for reader-controlled conveniences such as saved reading,
        listening progress, and “new since your last visit,” plus session storage for the current
        search state. External services reached through links may use their own analytics, cookies,
        or storage.
      </p>
      <h2 id="copyright-and-reuse">Copyright and reuse</h2>
      <p>
        Public access does not itself grant permission to republish material. Follow any rights or
        licence notice attached to an item. Source material and linked third-party work may have
        separate rights. For permission or a rights concern, identify the material and intended use
        through the <a href={sitePath("/contact/")}>contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>No default reuse licence is granted beyond any item-specific notice.</p>
      <h2>Disclosures</h2>
      <h3>Authorship</h3>
      <p>
        Independent Observer is a single-author research and media project by Siddhartha Harsh
        Wardhan. The site’s papers, previews, and adaptations have no external peer review unless a
        specific page explicitly records otherwise.
      </p>
      <h3>Funding</h3>
      <p>A funding statement has not yet been published.</p>
      <h3>Revenue</h3>
      <p>Supporting membership is planned but is not available for purchase on this site.</p>
      <h3>Conflicts of interest</h3>
      <p>A conflicts-of-interest statement has not yet been published.</p>
      <h3>Use of AI tools</h3>
      <p>
        A statement identifying AI tools used in the research and how their output is reviewed has
        not yet been published.
      </p>
      <p>
        Links to source institutions or distribution platforms do not imply endorsement. Historical
        downloads and views are dated distribution signals, not evidence of scholarly quality.
        Publication status is stated on each record.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .review-date {
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .status-definitions dt {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .status-definitions dd {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
  }
  .todo-notice {
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
    background: var(--paper-muted, #f4f1e8);
  }
</style>
